      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's the muddy, salty water from last time. We want two things back out of it, dry sand and dry salt. The trick is to use the property that's different. Sand is insoluble, which means it doesn't dissolve in water. Salt is soluble. It dissolves, and its particles spread out through the water. So how can we recover an insoluble solid and a dissolved solid from one mixture?",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
