        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Start with the sand. We'll pour the mixture through filter paper. Filter paper is full of tiny holes, called pores. Water molecules are far smaller than the pores, so they pass straight through. The dissolved salt is split into separate ions, which are tiny too, so they go through with the water. But a sand grain is a huge clump of particles, much too big for the pores, so it gets trapped. That's filtration. It separates an insoluble solid from a liquid, by particle size.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
