      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's the setup. Fold the filter paper into a cone, sit it in a funnel, and stand the funnel in a conical flask. Pour the mixture slowly down a glass rod, so it runs onto the paper without splashing. The solid left on the paper is called the residue. The liquid that drips through into the flask is called the filtrate.",
