          "score": 0.457
        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Now finish the sand. It's still wet, and that water is salt water. If you dried it now, salt crystals would be left stuck to the grains. So rinse the residue with a little distilled water, which has nothing dissolved in it. The fresh water carries the dissolved salt through the paper into the filtrate. Then dry the sand in a warm oven, or in the air, until it's completely dry. That's the insoluble solid recovered.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
    {
      "id": "solubility-saturation",
      "audio": "public/audio/chem-y11-m1-v03/solubility-saturation.wav",
