        {
          "word": "here's",
          "start": 0.824,
          "end": 1.106,
          "score": 0.29
        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "So here's crystallisation. Pour the filtrate into an evaporating basin, and heat it gently. The water evaporates, but the salt can't, so the solution gets more and more concentrated. Once it's saturated, the water that's left can't hold all the salt, and the extra salt comes out of the solution as solid crystals. Stop heating while there's still some liquid left, and let it cool. Then filter off the crystals, rinse them with a tiny amount of cold water, and dry them.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
    {
      "id": "surprise-solubility",
      "audio": "public/audio/chem-y11-m1-v03/surprise-solubility.wav",
