      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Filter first. The sand is insoluble and too big for the pores, so it stays as the residue. Rinse it with a little distilled water, then dry it. Next, heat the filtrate to concentrate it, and let it cool slowly. Potassium nitrate is much less soluble when it's cold, so crystals form. Filter them off and dry them. Crystallising before filtering is the slip to avoid.",
