      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "No, it's still salt water. The salt's ions went straight through the paper with the water, so the filtrate is a solution, a liquid with something dissolved in it. Clear only tells you nothing undissolved is floating in it. Put a drop on a warm watch glass, and when the water evaporates, tiny white crystals are left behind. Filtration can't remove a dissolved solid, and clear doesn't mean pure.",
