      "requestAttempts": 2,
      "pronunciationText": "Crystallisation does more than recover the salt. It also makes it purer. As a crystal grows, its ions fit into a neat, repeating lattice. Particles of other dissolved substances don't fit that pattern, so most of them stay in the leftover liquid, which is called the mother liquor. Slow cooling helps, because the crystals grow larger and more ordered, and trap less liquid. Boil it right down to dryness instead, and every dissolved impurity ends up in your solid.",
